---
description: Durable worktree, remote backup, and verification workflow
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow the Local agent workflow in AGENTS.md. Editing worktrees must be made
with `python3 scripts/agent_worktree.py <task-name>` and must never live under
`/tmp`; the creator establishes the remote branch automatically. Detached
`/tmp` snapshots are only for disposable tests, previews, and bisects.

Before stopping, checkpoint unfinished work with a commit and push. Before
reporting completion, run
`python3 scripts/agent_worktree.py --verify .`; it must confirm a clean tree
whose exact HEAD exists on the remote. Report the branch and commit SHA.

Run focused tests through scripts/ci.sh and use scripts/app_driver.py for
headless UI checks. Full PR checks run in GitHub CI. One task lands as one
commit; squash private checkpoint commits before review, using
`--force-with-lease` only on your own unmerged `codex/*` branch.
